From: mingzq <north_sea@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:13:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rk35xx: fail-safe default environment for OTA rescue routing

The single-copy U-Boot env blob (0x3f8000, no redundant copy) can lose
its CRC when saveenv hits a power cut mid-write. In that state U-Boot
falls back to the compiled default environment, which must fail SAFE:
route into the independent OTA Rescue assets -- the ext4 /recovery/
directory (plain recovery builds) or the signed FIT on the dedicated
PARTLABEL=recovery partition (raw-FIT secure builds) -- instead of
running distro_bootcmd across arbitrary media.

- embed the rescue script pair in the default env -- ota_rescue_boot_fs
  (ext4load/booti from boot partition 1) and ota_rescue_boot_fit
  (vendor boot_fit from the PARTLABEL=recovery partition, mirroring the
  A/B raw-fit slot boot), chained behind the ota_rescue_boot dispatcher
  (the only key its default bootcmd consumes); the transactional keys
  (ota_in_progress/ota_boot_next/ota_normal_boot) ride in the prefilled
  env blob, and fw_env tools read that blob, never this compiled default
- redefine the default bootcmd to "run ota_rescue_boot"

ota_rescue_boot is self-routing: the fs branch falls through when boot
partition 1 carries no ext4 /recovery/ assets (raw-FIT and A/B builds),
the fit branch falls through when no recovery partition exists (plain
and A/B builds), and the chain lands in "run distro_bootcmd". The patch
is therefore inert on every build flavor and is staged unconditionally:
no compile-time gating, and one stable U-Boot artifact hash across
flavors sharing a checkout.

The persistent (prefilled) env carries the full transactional bootcmd;
this default is its CRC-failure fallback (Seeed recovery OTA v0.8,
design section 3.4).

---
--- a/include/configs/rk3576_common.h
+++ b/include/configs/rk3576_common.h
@@ -77,13 +77,34 @@
 
 #include <config_distro_bootcmd.h>
 
+/*
+ * Seeed OTA rescue routing (v0.8 design section 3.4): the single-copy env
+ * blob at 0x3f8000 can lose its CRC when saveenv hits a power cut. The
+ * compiled default environment must fail SAFE in that case -- boot the
+ * independent Rescue (ext4 /recovery/ assets on plain builds, the signed
+ * FIT on the PARTLABEL=recovery partition on raw-FIT secure builds), or
+ * distro_bootcmd without either. Only the rescue scripts live here (the
+ * default bootcmd is their sole consumer); console is hardcoded to the
+ * rk35xx serial line like the other two copies -- build-time prefill and
+ * fwenv re-injection -- so the three cannot drift: an env-script
+ * ${console} evaluates empty and blinds the rescue console.
+ */
+#define OTA_RESCUE_ENV_SETTINGS \
+	"ota_rescue_boot_fs=ext4load ${devtype} ${devnum}:1 ${kernel_addr_r} /recovery/Image && ext4load ${devtype} ${devnum}:1 ${ramdisk_addr_r} /recovery/uInitrd && ext4load ${devtype} ${devnum}:1 ${fdt_addr_r} /recovery/board.dtb && setenv bootargs \"root=LABEL=armbi_root rootwait rootfstype=ext4 console=ttyFIQ0,1500000n8 armbian.bootdev=${devtype} armbian.bootdevnum=${devnum} armbian.ota_role=recovery\" && booti ${kernel_addr_r} ${ramdisk_addr_r} ${fdt_addr_r}\0" \
+	"ota_rescue_boot_fit=setenv boot_fit_part recovery; setenv bootargs \"root=/dev/mapper/armbian-root rw rootwait rootfstype=ext4 console=ttyFIQ0,1500000n8 armbian.bootdev=${devtype} armbian.bootdevnum=${devnum} armbian.ota_role=recovery\"; boot_fit\0" \
+	"ota_rescue_boot=run ota_rescue_boot_fs || run ota_rescue_boot_fit || run distro_bootcmd\0"
+
 #define CONFIG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS \
 	ENV_MEM_LAYOUT_SETTINGS \
 	"fdtfile=" FDTFILE \
 	"partitions=" PARTS_RKIMG \
 	ROCKCHIP_DEVICE_SETTINGS \
 	RKIMG_DET_BOOTDEV \
+	OTA_RESCUE_ENV_SETTINGS \
 	BOOTENV
+
+#undef CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND
+#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND "run ota_rescue_boot"
 #endif /* !CONFIG_SPL_BUILD */
 
 /* rockchip ohci host driver */
--- a/include/configs/rk3588_common.h
+++ b/include/configs/rk3588_common.h
